{"text": "INVESTIGATION OF THE POSSIBLE ENDOGENOUS FORMATION OF\n4-(METHYLNITROSAMINO)-1-(3-PYRIDYL)-1-BUTANONE (NNK)\n\nAuthors: G. Scherer und A.R. Tricker\nDate: May 1994\n\n1. Background\n\nFor several years the endogenous nitrosation of nicotine to yield 4-(methyinitrosa-\nmino}-1-(3-pyridyll-1-butanone (NNK) has been speculated to occur by Hoffmann\nat the American Health Foundation. However, no experimental evidence exists to\nsupport this speculation [1-6]. Our own studies which investigated the possible in\nvivo formation of 4-(N-methylnitrosamino)-4-(3-pyridyl}butyric acid (Iso-NNAC}\nfrom both the nitrosation of nicotine (via 4-(N-methylnitrosamino)-4-(3-pyridy!)-1-\nbutanal, NNA) or cotinine (via hydrolysis to cotinine acid), provided no evidence to\nsupport that nicotine or its main metabolite, cotinine, are subject to endogenous\nnitrosation {7]. Re-analysis of the urine samples collected for Iso-NNAC determina-\n\ntion in abstinent smokers receiving either buccal nicotine capsules (12-40 mg\n\n\u2018otine} or oral cotinine (60 mg) failed to show the presence of 4-(methyinitrosa-\nmino)-1-{3-pyridyll-1-butanol (NNAL) and its glucuronide conjugate (NNAL-Gluc),\n\u2018two metabolites of NNK (Tricker, unpublished results). At the time of analysis, the\ndetection limit for both NNAL and NNAL-Gluc in urine was 10 ng/l, 10-fold higher\nthan the current limit of detection using a modified analytical method. Using the\nabove method for nicotine administration, a nicotine plasma concentration of 32.4\ng/ml was achieved and the 24h urinary excretion ranged from 0.15-0.68 mg\n\nnicotine/day and 0.35-1.06 mg cotinine/day, considerably lower than the urinary\nexcretion observed in smokers (nicotine: 1.91 + 2.58, range 0.33-10.1 mg/day;\n\ncotinine: 1.83 1.18, range 0.44-4.41 mg/day) investigated in the same study.\n\nTherefore, both the sensitivity of the analytical mothod used and the systemic\ndose of nicotine may have been to low to allow detection of a possible endoge-\nnous nitrosation of nicotine to yield NNK and excretion of its NNAL and NNAL-Glue\n\nmetabolites in urine.\n\nbEGOTLEZOZ", "words": [{"text": "INVESTIGATION", "x0": 137, "y0": 122, "x1": 256, "y1": 134, "conf": 96.0}, {"text": "OF", "x0": 263, "y0": 122, "x1": 283, "y1": 134, "conf": 96.0}, {"text": "THE", "x0": 288, "y0": 122, "x1": 317, "y1": 134, "conf": 96.0}, {"text": "POSSIBLE", "x0": 324, "y0": 122, "x1": 395, "y1": 134, "conf": 96.0}, {"text": "ENDOGENOUS", "x0": 402, "y0": 122, "x1": 506, "y1": 134, "conf": 96.0}, {"text": "FORMATION", "x0": 513, "y0": 123, "x1": 602, "y1": 135, "conf": 96.0}, {"text": "OF", "x0": 609, "y0": 124, "x1": 628, "y1": 136, "conf": 93.0}, {"text": "4-(METHYLNITROSAMINO)-1-(3-PYRIDYL)-1-BUTANONE", "x0": 155, "y0": 149, "x1": 562, "y1": 162, "conf": 63.0}, {"text": "(NNK)", "x0": 571, "y0": 150, "x1": 611, "y1": 163, "conf": 88.0}, {"text": "Authors:", "x0": 254, "y0": 198, "x1": 306, "y1": 207, "conf": 33.0}, {"text": "G.", "x0": 332, "y0": 198, "x1": 346, "y1": 207, "conf": 72.0}, {"text": "Scherer", "x0": 352, "y0": 198, "x1": 398, "y1": 208, "conf": 95.0}, {"text": "und", "x0": 403, "y0": 198, "x1": 425, "y1": 208, "conf": 92.0}, {"text": "A.R.", "x0": 431, "y0": 198, "x1": 457, "y1": 208, "conf": 77.0}, {"text": "Tricker", "x0": 463, "y0": 198, "x1": 504, "y1": 208, "conf": 77.0}, {"text": "Date:", "x0": 250, "y0": 212, "x1": 286, "y1": 240, "conf": 96.0}, {"text": "May", "x0": 332, "y0": 221, "x1": 359, "y1": 233, "conf": 91.0}, {"text": "1994", "x0": 365, "y0": 221, "x1": 397, "y1": 231, "conf": 96.0}, {"text": "1.", "x0": 135, "y0": 292, "x1": 146, "y1": 301, "conf": 64.0}, {"text": "Background", "x0": 175, "y0": 291, "x1": 247, "y1": 304, "conf": 72.0}, {"text": "For", "x0": 134, "y0": 338, "x1": 154, "y1": 347, "conf": 96.0}, {"text": "several", "x0": 158, "y0": 338, "x1": 201, "y1": 347, "conf": 94.0}, {"text": "years", "x0": 206, "y0": 340, "x1": 238, "y1": 350, "conf": 96.0}, {"text": "the", "x0": 242, "y0": 